# myshell: a Unix shell implemented in C++ using Flex (lexer) and Bison (parser)

## compatibility:
- runs on Linux and macOS
- subshell ($()) and process substitution (<()) are Linux-only because of a dependency on /proc/self/exe

## features:
- command parsing and execution via Flex/Bison
- pipes and I/O redirection (stdin, stdout, stderr)
- built-in commands: cd, printenv, setenv, unsetenv, source
- signal handling (ctrl+c, zombie process elimination)
- quote and escape character handling
- subshell execution
- environment variable expansion
- tilde expansion
- wildcard globbing in the current directory
- interactive line editor with command history

## known limitations:
- wildcard globbing in subdirectories is not yet supported
